<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <title><%= content_for(:title) || "NL Screen demo" %></title>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
    <%# A static file has no asset server, so the stylesheet is inlined. %>
    <style><%= Rails.root.join("app/assets/stylesheets/application.css").read.html_safe %></style>
  </head>

  <body>
    <header>
      <a class="brand" href="index.html">NL Screen</a>
      <span class="tagline">static demo, snapshot of <%= @built_on.to_fs(:long) %></span>
    </header>
    <main>
      <p class="notes">
        A frozen snapshot of what the Rails app shows for a few example screens, using
        <%= @data_source %>. The real app (Turbo, Solid Queue, live streaming results)
        needs a Ruby server; run it locally with <code>bin/dev</code>.
      </p>
      <%= yield %>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
